{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    long int start;\n    long int total;\n} bucket;\n\nstatic void sort_bucket(char *strings, bucket *current, long int *indices,\n                        long int *scratch, int length) {\n    long int count = current->total;\n    long int start = current->start;\n    long int *src = indices;\n    long int *dst = scratch;\n    int pos;\n\n    if (count < 2 || length <= 1)\n        return;\n\n    for (pos = length - 1; pos > 0; --pos) {\n        size_t counts[256] = {0};\n        size_t next[256];\n        size_t prefix = 0;\n        long int j;\n        int c;\n\n        for (j = 0; j < count; ++j) {\n            unsigned char key = (unsigned char)strings[(size_t)src[start + j] * (size_t)length + (size_t)pos];\n            ++counts[key];\n        }\n\n        for (c = 0; c < 256; ++c) {\n            next[c] = prefix;\n            prefix += counts[c];\n        }\n\n        for (j = 0; j < count; ++j) {\n            unsigned char key = (unsigned char)strings[(size_t)src[start + j] * (size_t)length + (size_t)pos];\n            dst[start + next[key]++] = src[start + j];\n        }\n\n        {\n            long int *tmp = src;\n            src = dst;\n            dst = tmp;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (src != indices)\n        memcpy(indices + start, src + start, sizeof(*indices) * (size_t)count);\n}\n\nstatic long int *bucket_sort(char *strings, int length, long int size,\n                             int offset, int nbuckets) {\n    long int *returns;\n    long int *scratch;\n    long int *cursor;\n    bucket *buckets;\n    long int prefix = 0;\n    long int nonempty_buckets = 0;\n    long int i;\n\n    if (size <= 0)\n        return NULL;\n    if (nbuckets <= 0) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR buckets\\n\", stderr);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    returns = malloc(sizeof(*returns) * (size_t)size);\n    scratch = malloc(sizeof(*scratch) * (size_t)size);\n    buckets = calloc((size_t)nbuckets, sizeof(*buckets));\n    cursor = malloc(sizeof(*cursor) * (size_t)nbuckets);\n    if (returns == NULL || scratch == NULL || buckets == NULL || cursor == NULL) {\n        free(returns);\n        free(scratch);\n        free(buckets);\n        free(cursor);\n        fputs(\"ERROR memory\\n\", stderr);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\n        int which = (int)(unsigned char)strings[(size_t)i * (size_t)length] - offset;\n        ++buckets[which].total;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; ++i) {\n        buckets[i].start = prefix;\n        cursor[i] = prefix;\n        prefix += buckets[i].total;\n        if (buckets[i].total != 0)\n            ++nonempty_buckets;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\n        int which = (int)(unsigned char)strings[(size_t)i * (size_t)length] - offset;\n        returns[cursor[which]++] = i;\n    }\n\n    /* Each bucket owns a disjoint index range and scratch range. */\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic, 1) if (size >= 1024 && nonempty_buckets > 1)\n    for (long int bucket_index = 0; bucket_index < nbuckets; ++bucket_index)\n        sort_bucket(strings, &buckets[bucket_index], returns, scratch, length);\n\n    free(cursor);\n    free(buckets);\n    free(scratch);\n    return returns;\n}\n\nstatic void load(char **vString, long int *N, int *l, int *os, int *nb) {\n    int len;\n    int offset;\n    int nbucket;\n    long int n;\n    long int i;\n    char *strings;\n\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &len) != 1) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR len\\n\", stdout);\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &n) != 1) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR n\\n\", stdout);\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset) != 1) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR offset\\n\", stdout);\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbucket) != 1) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR nbucket\\n\", stdout);\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    ++nbucket;\n    ++len;\n    strings = n > 0 ? calloc((size_t)n, (size_t)len) : NULL;\n    if (n > 0 && strings == NULL) {\n        fputs(\"ERROR memory\\n\", stderr);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (size_t)i * (size_t)len) != 1) {\n            fprintf(stdout, \"ERROR %ld\\n\", i);\n            exit(1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    *vString = strings;\n    *N = n;\n    *l = len;\n    *os = offset;\n    *nb = nbucket;\n}\n\nstatic void save(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (size_t)index[i] * (size_t)len);\n}\n\nint main(int ac, char **av) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    long int N = 0;\n    long int *index = NULL;\n    int len = 0;\n    int offset;\n    int nbuckets;\n\n    (void)ac;\n    (void)av;\n    load(&strings, &N, &len, &offset, &nbuckets);\n    index = bucket_sort(strings, len, N, offset, nbuckets);\n    save(strings, index, N, len);\n\n    free(strings);\n    free(index);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","path":"src/bucketsort.c"}],"hypothesis":"Combining exact prefix-packed bucket ranges and stable suffix radix passes with thresholded dynamic parallel bucket sorting should retain the measured radix candidate's sorting efficiency while using available CPU cores when multiple substantial buckets exist.","notes":"Radix ordering relies on zero-initialized fixed-width string slots so NUL padding sorts consistently with strcmp. No commands were executed; correctness and performance remain for controller evaluation.","sources_kept":["8e11618e12bb4139","a8fba704a60d440d"],"transformations":["Count bucket populations, prefix-sum them into compact disjoint ranges, and scatter input indices into those ranges.","Use stable least-significant-byte counting passes over each bucket's string suffix with reusable scratch storage; zero-initialize string slots to preserve strcmp ordering for shorter strings.","Dynamically parallelize independent bucket sorts only for sufficiently large inputs with multiple nonempty buckets, and release temporary bucket and scratch storage afterward."]}